<i>And the man Mia loves will disappear.</i>

18:05.390 --> 18:06.600
<i>All is well.</i>

18:07.480 --> 18:10.200
I'll send you the money once you move out.

18:11.590 --> 18:12.980
What is it?

18:13.890 --> 18:16.990
I appreciate your thoughtfulness, Kagura-san.

18:18.240 --> 18:20.250
But I must decline!

18:20.740 --> 18:24.830
What? You're refusing my generous offer?

18:24.830 --> 18:27.530
On top of the debt your father left you,

18:27.530 --> 18:31.230
you owe money for kissing Tsukuyo-san, 
repairing that scooter and truck...

18:31.230 --> 18:33.250
What? How do you know about all that?

18:33.250 --> 18:37.020
And most importantly, 
how are you going to pay to have

18:37.020 --> 18:39.440
the principal figure repaired? 
You're running out of time.

18:39.440 --> 18:42.510
Do you have some kind of plan 
to get out of this situation?

18:42.510 --> 18:45.270
It's all right! I'll figure something out!

18:46.310 --> 18:47.770
What makes you say that?

18:47.770 --> 18:50.570
I've just got a feeling 
everything will be fine.

18:50.570 --> 18:53.610
You're just not facing reality.

18:53.610 --> 18:56.780
Perhaps you should tone down 
your meat-headedness.

18:56.780 --> 18:59.000
I won't allow you to continue 
insulting Yuzuki-san!

18:59.000 --> 19:00.780
I'm talking about you.

19:01.160 --> 19:04.980
It's true that our money problems would 
be solved for the present if I moved out.

19:04.980 --> 19:08.860
But that would merely be a temporary solution.

19:08.860 --> 19:12.780
And you may eventually find yourself 
facing the same situation again.

19:12.780 --> 19:13.790
Yes.

19:13.790 --> 19:18.550
Besides, I swore I'd support 
Yuzuki-san, no matter what.

19:19.720 --> 19:21.690
There must be something I can do.

19:21.690 --> 19:24.550
So I don't want to run away.

19:25.640 --> 19:27.640
<i>There's no point in continuing.</i>

19:28.350 --> 19:32.060
I see. Then I'll withdraw my offer for now.

19:32.060 --> 19:36.830
<i>Raising money isn't easy. I'm sure
he'll come back crying before long.</i>

19:36.830 --> 19:38.070
Good.

19:38.400 --> 19:40.570
Now I can keep my promise to Mia-san, too.

19:42.070 --> 19:44.450
We swore we'd fight together.

19:45.250 --> 19:45.950
What?

19:45.950 --> 19:47.950
I can't betray her.

19:47.950 --> 19:50.380
<i>Promise? Can't betray her?</i>

19:50.380 --> 19:52.020
<i>How dare you?</i>

19:52.710 --> 19:55.960
<i>You're in love with Aoba Yuzuki.</i>

19:56.270 --> 19:59.960
<i>Mia-san may not realize it herself, 
but she's genuinely in love with you.</i>

19:59.960 --> 20:01.660
<i>But that love can never be.</i>

20:01.660 --> 20:03.970
<i>What will she do once she realizes that?</i>

20:03.970 --> 20:07.820
<i>She may be so deeply wounded 
that she'll never get over it.</i>

20:10.340 --> 20:11.480
Kagura-san?

20:11.480 --> 20:15.230
Don't talk about Mia-san like you know her!

20:15.230 --> 20:16.890
You can't even take responsibility for her!

20:16.890 --> 20:19.050
You're openly expressing your anger!

20:19.050 --> 20:20.110
What?!

20:20.110 --> 20:22.860
I've never seen you so emotional before.

20:22.860 --> 20:24.990
I'm not mad at all!

20:24.990 --> 20:27.130
But you're even raising your voice.

20:27.130 --> 20:29.500
I'm not raising my voice at all!

20:30.210 --> 20:31.620
What's so funny?!

20:31.620 --> 20:35.960
I'm relieved you can get 
so upset on Mia-san's behalf.

20:35.960 --> 20:38.120
I told you, I'm not upset.

20:38.120 --> 20:42.680
You care about Mia-san more than 
you care about her family circumstances.

20:44.090 --> 20:49.440
Something seemed off to me 
about you betraying Mia-san.

20:49.440 --> 20:51.580
What are you talking about?

20:51.580 --> 20:57.000
After all, when you smile at each other, 
you seem genuinely happy.

20:58.240 --> 21:04.860
This wasn't a betrayal. You acted 
because you care so deeply about Mia-san.

21:04.860 --> 21:06.140
N-No—

21:06.140 --> 21:07.870
That's why you—

21:15.760 --> 21:18.580
Ugh, I kicked something I shouldn't have.

21:16.830 --> 21:18.580
<b><i>Antibacterial
Spray</i></b>

21:18.580 --> 21:21.440
I'm simply loyal to my job.

21:21.440 --> 21:25.580
In the name of the Baldwin family, 
I shall carry out my plan.

21:25.580 --> 21:28.550
I don't know how you got confused.

21:35.980 --> 21:37.450
Kagura!

21:37.450 --> 21:40.190
Thank you for waiting, everyone.

21:40.190 --> 21:41.850
Have you seen Akagami?

21:41.850 --> 21:43.780
He's gone to sleep.

21:44.560 --> 21:46.950
Good timing, Kagura.

21:47.260 --> 21:52.170
Do you know any ways to make money quick?

21:52.170 --> 21:54.950
I've been asking everyone for advice, but...

21:54.950 --> 21:56.060
Uh...

21:56.060 --> 21:59.830
You can count on her. 
My Kagura is highly dependable.

21:59.830 --> 22:03.660
After all, she and I are best friends. 
We're practically the same person!

22:04.840 --> 22:06.740
Right, Kagura?

22:08.420 --> 22:09.640
<i>Good grief.</i>

22:10.090 --> 22:12.580
<i>I'm just doing my job.</i>

23:45.060 --> 23:47.450
The flames of love are cackling.

23:45.060 --> 24:00.080
<b>Next Time

I Just Got a Little Excited</b>

23:47.450 --> 23:49.400
You mean "crackling."

23:49.400 --> 23:51.480
Your heart is crackling for Akagami-san.

23:51.480 --> 23:53.520
My heart's not pounding for Akagami!

23:53.520 --> 23:56.550
I just got... a little excited.

23:56.550 --> 23:59.660
Then let's hear you sing about it.
